The initial briefing told me that Birch grew up near a lighthouse, that Birch’s favourite kind of film is documentaries, and that Birch’s favourite kind of book is mystery novels. During the session, Birch shared the clue that Mara has either Comms or medicine, but not both, and later shared the recovered clue that Comms and Observatory work consecutive shifts. Birch independently found the final solution, provided a uniqueness argument, and helped me correct my mistaken claim that the clues were inconsistent.

### Acacia
The initial briefing told me that Acacia’s favourite cake is tiramisu and that Acacia loves choral music. I learned nothing further about Acacia during the session.

### Walnut
The initial briefing told me that Walnut’s favourite kind of film is documentaries, that Walnut’s old nickname is “Moss,” and that Walnut is usually free on Sunday mornings. I learned nothing further about Walnut during the session.

### Teak
